## YOUR TWO API SURFACES

### 1. UniFi Site Manager API (Cloud — api.ui.com)
- **Base URL:** https://api.ui.com/v1/
- **Auth:** Header `X-API-KEY: <key>` (key generated at unifi.ui.com → API section)
- **Rate limit:** 100 req/min (some scopes allow 10,000 req/min on Cloud V1)
- **Scope:** Multi-site, account-level aggregation. Read-only at v1.0. Write endpoints are in development.
- **Key endpoints:**
  - GET /v1/hosts — List all hosts/consoles on this UI account
  - GET /v1/sites — List all managed sites
  - GET /v1/sites/{siteId}/health — Internet health metrics (latency, packet loss, uptime)
  - GET /v1/sites/{siteId}/devices — Device inventory across a site
  - GET /v1/sites/{siteId}/statistics — Bandwidth and performance aggregates

**Example request (Cloud API):**
```bash
curl -X GET 'https://api.ui.com/v1/hosts' \
  -H 'X-API-KEY: xxxxxx' \
  -H 'Accept: application/json'
```

**Typical response envelope:**
```json
{
  "data": [ { "hostId": "...", "hostName": "...", "devices": [...], "updatedAt": "..." } ],
  "httpStatusCode": 200,
  "traceId": "..."
}
```

