### 2. UniFi Network Local API (On-Prem — Dream Machine / Controller)
- **Base URL (UDM Pro/SE/Max):** https://<console-ip>/proxy/network/
- **Base URL (legacy controller):** https://<controller-ip>:8443/
- **Auth:** POST to `/api/auth/login` with `{"username":"...","password":"..."}`, store session cookie. UDM uses `/api/auth/login`; legacy controller uses `/api/login`.
- **Rate limit:** None enforced locally, but be respectful.
- **Scope:** Per-site, per-device, full read/write. Site slug is `{site}` (usually `default`).
- **REST pattern:** Base endpoints support GET/POST/PUT/DELETE. PUT requires the object `_id`. POST to base creates; PUT to `/{id}` updates.
- **Command pattern:** POST to `api/s/{site}/cmd/<manager>` with `{"cmd":"<command>"}`.

**Key endpoint groups:**
| Path | Methods | Description |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `api/s/{site}/stat/health` | GET | Dashboard health — WAN, LAN, WLAN subsystem status |
| `api/s/{site}/stat/sta` | GET | Active client devices |
| `api/s/{site}/stat/device` | GET | All UniFi devices (AP, switch, gateway) |
| `api/s/{site}/stat/device-basic` | GET | Lightweight device list (mac, type only) |
| `api/s/{site}/rest/wlanconf` | GET/POST/PUT | Wireless network configurations |
| `api/s/{site}/rest/networkconf` | GET/POST/PUT | Site network/VLAN config |
| `api/s/{site}/rest/firewallrule` | GET/POST/PUT/DELETE | User-defined firewall rules |
| `api/s/{site}/rest/firewallgroup` | GET/POST/PUT | Firewall IP/port groups |
| `api/s/{site}/rest/routing` | GET | Static routes |
| `api/s/{site}/rest/portforward` | GET | Port forward rules |
| `api/s/{site}/rest/alarm` | GET | Active alarms |
| `api/s/{site}/stat/event` | GET | Event log |
| `api/s/{site}/stat/session` | GET | Client sessions (requires start/end UNIX timestamps) |
| `api/s/{site}/stat/sysinfo` | GET | Controller/console system info |
| `api/s/{site}/cmd/stamgr` | POST | Client management commands |
| `api/s/{site}/cmd/devmgr` | POST | Device management commands |

**UDM Pro auth + first call:**
```bash
# 1. Login
curl -k -X POST \
  -d '{"username":"admin","password":"secret"}' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -c /tmp/unifi.cookie \
  https://192.168.1.1/api/auth/login

# 2. Use cookie on subsequent calls
curl -k -X GET \
  -b /tmp/unifi.cookie \
  https://192.168.1.1/proxy/network/api/s/default/stat/health
```

**Response envelope (local API):**
```json
{
  "meta": { "rc": "ok" },
  "data": [ ... ]
}
```
Error: `{ "meta": { "rc": "error", "msg": "api.err.LoginRequired" }, "data": [] }`

