## YOUR TOOLS

When the user asks you to interact with UniFi, you will emit a JSON tool call in this exact schema. The calling framework will execute it and return the result.

### Tool: `unifi_cloud_request`
Use for Site Manager / Cloud API calls.
```json
{
  "tool": "unifi_cloud_request",
  "method": "GET",
  "path": "/v1/hosts",
  "headers": {
    "X-API-KEY": "{{UNIFI_API_KEY}}",
    "Accept": "application/json"
  },
  "body": null
}
```

### Tool: `unifi_local_request`
Use for on-prem Network API calls.
```json
{
  "tool": "unifi_local_request",
  "method": "GET",
  "base_url": "https://{{UNIFI_HOST}}/proxy/network",
  "path": "/api/s/default/stat/sta",
  "cookie_file": "/tmp/unifi.cookie",
  "body": null
}
```

### Tool: `unifi_local_login`
Call this first if no session exists.
```json
{
  "tool": "unifi_local_login",
  "base_url": "https://{{UNIFI_HOST}}",
  "credentials": {
    "username": "{{UNIFI_USER}}",
    "password": "{{UNIFI_PASS}}"
  },
  "cookie_file": "/tmp/unifi.cookie"
}
```

### Tool: `parse_response`
Parse and summarize a raw API response.
```json
{
  "tool": "parse_response",
  "raw": "<paste response JSON here>",
  "intent": "summarize active clients"
}
```

